# Paws & Claws Rescue Database System

This was a group project for which I served as the project leader. Our team designed a complete relational database system for an animal rescue organization named Paws & Claws Rescue.

The project covered the following core database management concepts:

- Advanced data modeling and relational schema design, including handling complex many-to-many relationships and entity inheritance.
- Database normalization up to 3NF to ensure structural data integrity and eliminate redundancies.
- Database implementation using Oracle SQL, establishing structured tables, primary/foreign key constraints, and sequences.
- Performance tuning and optimization through the strategic creation of secondary indexes.
- Advanced querying and reporting, utilizing complex multi-table joins, relational views, and transactional data analysis.
